Z||000007||fierobaby||08-19-2001||12:34 PM||||ok first off Lisa don't go yellin at me... I didn't blame anyone. The weather sucked and hey you know crap happens. But I hear about all these other clubs always getting stuff to do and going cool places... Which I know CF's does but very rarely do I see this club getting super excited about a darn thing. I just wanted to ask if anyone around here has a more active club. It also seems to me that there are not alot of Fieros around my area. Which is fine but I'm beginging to think I should start my own club because of what I want in a club I can't find. I am not trying to be rude to anyone here. I would just like more in a club than meetings every 2nd Thursday and people much older than I am. I feel like a little kid around them. thats all I was trying to a say Scott on the other hand was saying something completly different. Oh well whatever I am not apologizing for him its his tough crap. ok that was my 2 cents! now I say drop it cause I ment nothing harmful by this thread and do not wish to make anyone mad||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||08-19-2001||02:59 PM||||I enjoyed meeting you all baby. but I think the things you say like all the above might explain why people didnt show up. I go almost everywhere I say im going. I did go to Jollies yesterday, just didnt feel like seeing people get all lovey dovey all day. Look at the good side, you dont have to buy lunchmeat and bread for a long time. BTW we had a club road ralley that paid a bunch of money and was a great ez drive. we had 5 cars show and they were the checkpoint workers, and only 2 other people, one of them being Tweety-bird. And it was a perfect day, and not another show in the state going on. So I know a little how you feel. See ya around again Im sure.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Cheever3000||08-19-2001||04:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I'm beginging to think I should start my own club because of what I want in a club I can't find... I would just like more in a club than meetings every 2nd Thursday and people much older than I am.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I can sympathize with you a little.  My club is not all I'd like it to be, and the people are older just like you said (and I'm 44!).  But you know what? I'm making suggestions and bringing in new members and getting involved, and slowly it's making a difference.  I absolutely agree that a club should be more than the meetings - I will soon ask my club to consider taking turns with all of us going to members' houses to do any work they need on their car or garage or house, whatever they could use some extra help with.  Does anybody else's club do that?  I'd like to know if it works.  <P>I do feel bad for your no-show.  That's got to disappoint you.  Just bounce back, pitch in when others do theirs, and you'll eventually see people interested in coming to yours.<P>||||reg||1
